# How to cite the Post-Drug Syndromes Research Library.
# GitHub reads this file for its "Cite this repository" box, and Zenodo reads it
# when a release is deposited. Update `version`, `date-released` and the version
# DOI under `identifiers` with every corpus release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this library, please cite the release you used."
title: "Post-Drug Syndromes Research Library: a curated corpus on PFS, PSSD and post-retinoid syndrome"
abstract: >-
  A curated, cross-linked research library on post-finasteride syndrome (PFS),
  post-SSRI sexual dysfunction (PSSD) and post-retinoid syndrome. It holds
  peer-reviewed papers, regulatory documents, attributed clinician commentary,
  videos, community accounts, a glossary, a timeline, gene reference cards, a
  mechanism matrix rated separately for each syndrome, and a list of open
  questions. Every record carries a paraphrased summary, a verification status,
  links to its source and notes on how other records in the library bear on it.
  Releases are immutable and versioned. For research use only, not medical advice.
type: dataset
version: "1.55"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://postdrugsyndrome.com/research/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/uncSoft/post-drug-syndromes-corpus"
authors:
  - family-names: Taverna
    given-names: John
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
    website: "https://jtaverna.org/"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-9893-6893"
keywords:
  - post-finasteride syndrome
  - PFS
  - post-SSRI sexual dysfunction
  - PSSD
  - post-retinoid sexual dysfunction
  - PRSD
  - finasteride
  - isotretinoin
  - selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors
  - neurosteroids
  - allopregnanolone
  - androgen receptor
  - pharmacogenomics
  - pharmacovigilance
  - iatrogenic illness
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24142337"
    description: "Concept DOI: always resolves to the newest release"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24144288"
    description: "This release (v1.55)"
